   "title": "UK snow conditions, 16 November 2026: depth, fresh snow and the next days",
   "description": "UK snow today, 16 November: snow cover, new snow, snow depth by height, the next days and the best resorts.",
   "lede": "In the UK, about 5,740 km² of high ground is white today, 1,290 km² less than yesterday. In other words, 15 % of the mapped high ground is white.",
   "sections": [
    {
     "h": "Snow on the ground",
     "p": [
      "Most of the ground is white from about 800 m up. A week ago it was 270 km², so the cover has grown by 5,470 km²."
     ]
    },
    {
     "h": "Fresh snow",
     "p": [
      "Three-day totals peak at 6 cm, around the Northwest Highlands, the Cairngorms and Ben Nevis and Lochaber.",
      "At least 5 cm fell over some 800 km²."
     ]
    },
    {
     "h": "Low, middle and high ground",
     "p": [
      "Climb and the snow gets deeper: between 0 and 500 m, under 1 cm on average, 9 % covered; between 500 and 1,000 m, 1 cm on average, 31 % covered; between 1,000 and 1,500 m, 4 cm on average, 89 % covered."
     ]
    },
    {
     "h": "What it means on the slopes",
     "p": [
